:null,"first":"Richard L.","key":"peterspau","last":"Peters","name":"Peters, Richard L.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Patrick","key":"fontipau","last":"Fonti","name":"Fonti, Patrick","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"David C.","key":"frankpau","last":"Frank","name":"Frank, David C.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Rafael","key":"poyatospau","last":"Poyatos","name":"Poyatos, Rafael","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"first":"Christoforos","key":"pappaspau","last":"Pappas","name":"Pappas, Christoforos","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ansgar","key":"kahmenpau","last":"Kahmen","name":"Kahmen, Ansgar","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"6","corresponding":null,"first":"Vinicio","key":"carraropau","last":"Carraro","name":"Carraro, Vinicio","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"7","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Angela Luisa","key":"prendinpau","last":"Prendin","locid":"9e0fe9e9-be06-444f-bf55-c179b7bf8f87","name":"Prendin, Angela Luisa","orcid":"0000-0002-5809-7314","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Loic","key":"schneiderpau","last":"Schneider","name":"Schneider, Loic","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"8","corresponding":null,"first":"Jennifer L.","key":"baltzerpau","last":"Baltzer","name":"Baltzer, Jennifer L.","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"9","corresponding":null,"first":"Greg A.","key":"barongaffordpau","last":"Baron-Gafford","name":"Baron-Gafford, Greg A.","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lars","key":"dietrichpau","last":"Dietrich","name":"Dietrich, Lars","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"10","corresponding":null,"first":"Ingo","key":"heinrichpau","last":"Heinrich","name":"Heinrich, Ingo","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"9","corresponding":null,"first":"Rebecca L.","key":"minorpau","last":"Minor","name":"Minor, Rebecca L.","rank":14,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"first":"Oliver","key":"sonnentagpau","last":"Sonnentag","name":"Sonnentag, Oliver","rank":15,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"11","corresponding":null,"first":"Ashley M.","key":"mathenypau","last":"Matheny","name":"Matheny, Ashley M.","rank":16,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"12","corresponding":null,"first":"Maxwell G.","key":"wightmanpau","last":"Wightman","name":"Wightman, Maxwell G.","rank":17,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Kathy","key":"steppepau","last":"Steppe","name":"Steppe, Kathy","rank":18,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["29862531"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1111/nph.15241","issn":["0028646X","14698137"],"issn_org":["0028646X"],"issue":"4","journal":"New Phytologist","pages":"1283-1299","publisher":"Wiley-Blackwell Publishing Ltd","status":"p","title":"New Phytologist","volume":"219"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85051114507"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-cfbf88fd-c2eb-4bf5-9efc-46dbc1d51d4b"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Quantification of uncertainties in conifer sap flow measured with the thermal dissipation method","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-248032","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"OBJECTIVES: Treat-to-target recommendations have identified 'remission' as a target in systemic lupus erythematosus (SLE), but recognise that there is no universally accepted definition for this. Therefore, we initiated a process to achieve consensus on potential definitions for remission in SLE. METHODS: An international task force of 60 specialists and patient representatives participated in preparatory exercises, a face-to-face meeting and follow-up electronic voting. The level for agreement was set at 90%. RESULTS: The task force agreed on eight key statements regarding remission in SLE and three principles to guide the further development of remission definitions:1. Definitions of remission will be worded as follows: remission in SLE is a durable state characterised by …………………. (reference to symptoms, signs, routine labs).2. For defining remission, a validated index must be used, for example, clinical systemic lupus erythematosus disease activity index (SLEDAI)=0, British Isles lupus assessment group (BILAG) 2004 D/E only, clinical European consensus lupus outcome measure (ECLAM)=0; with routine laboratory assessments included, and supplemented with physician's global assessment.3. Distinction is made between remission off and on therapy: remission off therapy requires the patient to be on no other treatment for SLE than maintenance antimalarials; and remission on therapy allows patients to be on stable maintenance antimalarials, low-dose corticosteroids (prednisone ≤5 mg/day), maintenance immunosuppressives and/or maintenance biologics.The task force also agreed that the most appropriate outcomes (dependent variables) for testing the prognostic value (construct validity) of potential remission definitions are: death, damage, flares and measures of health-related quality of life. CONCLUSIONS: The work of this international task force provides a framework for testing different definitions of remission against long-term outcomes.","author_count":58,"contributors":["van Vollenhoven, Ronald","Voskuyl, Alexandre","Bertsias, George","Aranow, Cynthia","Aringer, Martin","Arnaud, Laurent","Askanase, Anca","Balážová, Petra","Bonfa, Eloisa","Bootsma, Hendrika","Boumpas, Dimitrios","Bruce, Ian","Cervera, Ricard","Clarke, Ann","Coney, Cindy","Costedoat-Chalumeau, Nathalie","Czirják, László","Derksen, Ronald","Doria, Andrea","Dörner, Thomas","Fischer-Betz, Rebecca","Fritsch-Stork, Ruth","Gordon, Caroline","Graninger, Winfried","Györi, Noémi","Houssiau, Frédéric","Isenberg, David","Jacobsen, Søren","Jayne, David","Kuhn, Annegret","Le Guern, Veronique","Lerstrøm, Kirsten","Levy, Roger","Machado-Ribeiro, Francinne","Mariette, Xavier","Missaykeh, Jamil","Morand, Eric","Mosca, Marta","Inanc, Murat","Navarra, Sandra","Neumann, Irmgard","Olesinska, Marzena","Petri, Michelle","Rahman, Anisur","Rekvig, Ole Petter","Rovensky, Jozef","Shoenfeld, Yehuda","Smolen, Josef","Tincani, Angela","Urowitz, Murray","van Leeuw, Bernadette","Vasconcelos, Carlos","Voss, Anne","Werth, Victoria P","Zakharova, Helena","Zoma, Asad","Schneider, Matthias","Ward, Michael"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-047199"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"51-200 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["America, North","America, South","Asia, Middle East","Asia, South","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD","Oceania"],"country":["Australia","Austria","Belgium","Brazil","Canada","France","Germany","Greece","Hungary","Israel","Italy","Lebanon","Netherlands","Norway","Philippines","Portugal","Russia","Slovakia","Spain","Sweden","Turkey","United Kingdom","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Botkin Hospital","Catholic University of Louvain","Charité - University Medicine Berlin","Corporal Michael J. Crescenz VA Medical Center","Department of Genetic Medicine, Manchester University NHS Foundation Trust, Manchester, United Kingdom.","Heinrich Heine University Düsseldorf","Hospital Clinic of Barcelona","H